SUMMARY:Courtesy Cross Post - Black Mountain Camino - Black Mountain Town 
 Square
DESCRIPTION:The Asheville Hiking Group\nPosting here as a courtesy for the
  Society of Pilgrims on the Camino .\n\nRoute: Loop around the town of Bla
 ck Mountain through charming neighborhoods and out to Montreat to enjoy th
 e frescos.\nSurface: Pavement and well maintained trails.\nPace: 3.2-3.4\n
 Elevation: estimate 500 feet\, in small chunks.\n\nSee details here: [http
 s://www.facebook.com/share/p/1cWbB2fN2n/](https://www.facebook.com/share/p
 /1cWbB2fN2n/)\n\nThe meeting spot is\nBlack Mountain Town Square at the ma
 in intersection downtown of State Street and Hwy 9.\n\n[https://maps.app.g
 oo.gl/LuD614YPpehztKKr8[https://maps.app.goo.gl/LuD614YPpehztKKr8](https:/
 /maps.app.goo.gl/LuD614YPpehztKKr8[https://maps.app.goo.gl/LuD614YPpehztKK
 r8)]([https://maps.app.goo.gl/LuD614YPpehztKKr8](https://maps.app.goo.gl/L
 uD614YPpehztKKr8))\n\nAbout 10.5 miles finishing around 1:30.\n\nIt is pos
 sible to cut it short at 4.5 miles or 8 miles.\n\nThere will be a coffee s
 top.\n\nPack a lunch\n\nLeader: Maurice Frank\, WNC American Pilgrims on t
 he Camino\n\nNo sign up - just show up.\n\nHere are the details for our up
 coming Black Mountain Camino walk on Saturday June 6 at 9:00 AM. As usual\
 , please arrive 10-15 minutes early.\n\nWe will meet at the Black Mountain
  Town Square pavilion located near the corner of Hwy 9 and State Street. F
 ree parking is adjacent to the town square.\n\nDirections and Parking: If 
 coming from Asheville take I-40 East to Exit 64 for Black Mountain\, Left 
 off the exit onto Hwy 9\; continue to the main intersection of Hwy 9 and S
 tate St\; Right onto E. State St\; first Left onto West Street\; Immediate
  left into Black Mountain Town Square parking lot. If this parking area is
  full you can park opposite the Police and Fire Dept building – also fre
 e but park on either end - - but not in the reserved spots in the middle. 
 A third free parking area is next to White Horse Black Mountain across the
  street from Town Square.\n\nOur full walk is about 10.5 miles and will ta
 ke about 4 hours. You can leave the walk early for a total distance of 4.5
  or 8 miles. The walk is moderate with only one section with noticeable el
 evation gain. Most of the walk is on paved surfaces so wear comfortable sh
 oes. Dress appropriately for the weather.\n\nSome highlights of the route 
 include Lake Tomahawk\, views of the Seven Sisters mountain peaks\, walkin
 g from town to town as on a Camino\, a church with a mural\, a short secti
 on in the woods\, bridge crossings\, and creekside walks. There is also an
  opportunity to become the King of England (you have to be there to unders
 tand).\n\nWe stop for coffee at Peri Social House at about 4.0 miles (appr
 oximately 10:15)\, then for lunch by Montreat College. Bring a packed lunc
 h.\n\nBring water and snacks. There are multiple restroom opportunities in
 cluding Black Mountain Town Square where we start and end.\n\nOptional bee
 rs afterwards at nearby Lookout Brewery on S. Ridgeway Ave. They have a fo
 od truck.\n\nNo RSVP required. Just show up and please arrive 10-15 minute
 s before the walk begins at 9:00 AM.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/ashevillehikinggroup/events/315092897
 /
